# Custom Checkstyle Checker Configuration

You can define a custom [Checker configuration xml file](https://checkstyle.org/config.html#Checker).
You can reference it through a URL, a file, or a build classpath resource.

Use the `configLocation` parameter to reference a custom Checkstyle Checker configuration.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <configLocation>checkstyle.xml</configLocation>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

This example makes the plugin check for a file named `checkstyle.xml`.
It can find the file in the compile scope of the dependencies or in the build extensions classpath.

The Checkstyle Plugin ships with two predefined configuration definitions.
It selects the Sun Microsystems definition by default.

- **sun_checks.xml** - Sun Microsystems Definition (default).
- **google_checks.xml** - Google Definition.
